<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">UNDERSTAND YOUR PERFORMANCE</div><h1>Scoring and CEFR</h1><p>A transparent 0–100 score for every language skill.</p></div></section><section class="container section prose"><h2>How scores are calculated</h2><p>Listening, Reading, Writing and Speaking each receive a whole-number score between 0 and 100. Your overall score is the arithmetic average of the four skills, rounded to the nearest whole number. There is no pass or fail.</p><div class="equation"><span>(Listening + Reading + Writing + Speaking) ÷ 4</span><strong>= Overall score</strong></div><h2>CEFR reference bands</h2><p>These score bands are maintained by GEST headquarters and may be revised for future results. They are an alignment to the Common European Framework of Reference (CEFR).</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Score</th><th scope="col">CEFR level</th></tr></thead><tbody><% bands.forEach(b=>{ %><tr><td><%= b.min_score %>–<%= b.max_score %></td><td><span class="level-pill"><%= b.label %></span></td></tr><% }) %></tbody></table></div><p>Receiving organisations should examine all four component scores as well as the overall score when making decisions.</p></section>
